Run cat >/tmp/pr-review-717.json <<'EOF'
{
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "## Review Summary\n\n**Task:** @01KK7T2C50AGJB393WNBK5CTHR\n**Spec:** @session-storage-modes\n\n### AC Coverage\n- [x] `ac-config`: tests cover accepted `local` and `branch` values\n- [ ] `ac-config-default`: current schema/test pair still leaves `sessions` undefined when the block is omitted, so local is not the parsed default\n- [ ] `ac-config-invalid`: tests do not assert that the validation message lists the valid values `local` and `branch`\n- [x] `ac-branch-name`: covered\n- [x] `ac-branch-name-default`: covered\n\n### Code / Spec Alignment\n- `ManifestSchema.parse({ kynetic: \"1.0\", project: { name: \"x\" } })` currently returns no `sessions` object, which does not satisfy the task note to default storage to `local` in schema output.\n\n### Regression Check\n- [x] `npm test` passed locally (`187` files, `4110` tests, `3` skipped)\n\nBlocking issues are noted inline below.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/schema/spec.ts",
      "line": 136,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: The whole `sessions` object is optional here, so omitting it leaves `ManifestSchema.parse(...)` with `sessions === undefined` instead of a defaulted `storage: \"local\"`. That conflicts with the task note (`Default storage to \"local\"`) and `@session-storage-modes ac-config-default`."
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/schema/session-storage-config.test.ts",
      "line": 65,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: This test is asserting the opposite of `@session-storage-modes ac-config-default`. Right now it locks in `sessions === undefined` when the block is omitted, but the task/spec require local mode to be the default when `sessions.storage` is absent."
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/schema/session-storage-config.test.ts",
      "line": 87,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: `@session-storage-modes ac-config-invalid` requires the validation message to indicate the valid values. This assertion only checks for `Invalid enum value`, so it does not verify that the message mentions `local` and `branch`."
    }
  ]
}
EOF

